# Golden Section Method

## Definition
The Golden Section Method is an optimization technique used to find the 
minimum of a unimodal function on a closed interval [a, b].

## Golden Ratio
The method is based on the golden ratio:

Whole segment / larger part = larger part / smaller part

Numerical value:
φ ≈ 1.618

## Choosing Points

Given an interval [a, b], we define:

x1 = a + 0.382(b - a)  
x2 = a + 0.618(b - a)

Also:
x2 = a + b - x1

## Algorithm

1. Compute f(x1) and f(x2)
2. If f(x1) ≤ f(x2), then the new interval is [a, x2]
3. If f(x1) > f(x2), then the new interval is [x1, b]
4. Repeat until (b - a) ≤ ε

## Final Result

The approximate minimum point is:

x* ≈ (a + b) / 2

## Advantages

- Does not require derivatives
- Stable and efficient
- Suitable for optimization problems
